  "worked_solution": "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3t-3 \\\\ 7-9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-3,7,-\\frac{1}{2})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
